# Environment variables for Weather MCP Server
# Copy this file to .env for local development (never commit .env!)

# =============================================================================
# Open-Meteo Configuration (DEFAULT - NO API KEY REQUIRED)
# =============================================================================
# Open-Meteo is the default weather provider and requires NO configuration.
# Just deploy and run! The following URLs are already hardcoded in weather_broker.py:
#   - Geocoding: https://geocoding-api.open-meteo.com/v1/search
#   - Forecast: https://api.open-meteo.com/v1/forecast
#
# Rate limit: ~10,000 calls/day (non-commercial use)
# Coverage: Global
# Documentation: https://open-meteo.com/en/docs

# No environment variables needed for Open-Meteo!

# =============================================================================
# Optional: Lakebase Postgres for MCP call tracking (database_tracker.py)
# =============================================================================
# If you want to log all MCP tool calls to Lakebase for observability:
# LAKEBASE_URL=postgresql://<role>:<password>@<your-lakebase-host>.database.cloud.databricks.com:5432/databricks_postgres?sslmode=require

# =============================================================================
# WeatherAPI.com Configuration (OPTIONAL UPGRADE)
# =============================================================================
# If you want to use WeatherAPI.com instead:
# 1. Sign up at https://www.weatherapi.com/signup.aspx (free tier: 1M calls/month)
# 2. Get your API key from the dashboard
# 3. Run setup_secrets.py to store the key securely
# WEATHER_API_PROVIDER=weatherapi
# WEATHER_API_KEY=your_weatherapi_key_here
